{
  "Comment": "Construction chains by lift family (keys are the lowercase LiftFamily names) and the run-building stages. Each stage becomes one task per unit on the job board: PerUnit tower/terminal/km/carrier/m3/lift/run. WorkHoursPerUnit is machine-hours at work rate 1.0; CostPerUnit is the subcontract/material cost on top of the lift capex; labour is WorkRequired x LaborRatePerHour x LaborCrew at stage completion. Stages with MaxWindKmh / MinTempC wait for a weather window (concrete cannot be poured below -5 C without heating; cranes and helicopters stop in 30-35 km/h). Helicopter tower setting flies a heavy-lift type at 6,500 USD per flight hour plus mobilisation; aerial families require it, other families may opt in when the line crosses the gorge. Figures follow 2020s Alpine lift-building practice: a 1 km fixed-grip chair is built in about 10-12 weeks of site work, a 3S in a full summer.",
